OWED: signed runtime `/` emits Zig `@divTrunc` (or equivalent), not bare `/`.

Never green on the 2026-08-26..09-07 boards. Parked so the failed
column means regression again. Driven by --todo-sweep; drop this
marker when the pin is promotable.

The `%` half of this shape landed 2026-09-17 (010_063 and 320_144/145/146
pin it); `/` still needs the operand type, so it is the ruling in
NEEDS_RULING that is outstanding, not the mechanism.


---

RULED 2026-10-24, under the host-leak doctrine (frag-the-host-is-an-emission-detail,
challenge 029): Koru owns `/`. A raw Zig error reaching the user is a host
leak; the surface semantic is the language's to own.

- Signed integer `/` lowers to `@divTrunc` — matching comptime_eval's
  "C-parity choice" already in the tree. The comptime-vs-runtime
  disagreement closes in comptime's favor; refusing would have inverted it.
- Float `/` stays `/` — exact division, no change.

Owed: the type oracle at the emit site (the NEEDS_RULING's named work) —
the emitter must know signed-int vs float to pick the lowering. This pin
flips green when that lands; the semantic is decided.
